why: the fact is a piece of the book's history and the site is a function combining two answers about a format; a writer on 2026-09-22 wrote the history and stopped, and a reviewer read the block and asked "and what?"; the block owes the tie: what `getFormatClaim` does about the fact, which is take either answer as `Accepted`, or fall back to the book's claim where the probe answers `Unknown`, since the probe lagging the book explains both acts; a function's body shows what the code does and cannot show that the fact is why, so the tie is never `shown by the body`
labelled: 2026-09-22
--- code
export function getFormatClaim(formatName: string): LedgerClaim {
  const bookClaim = getBookFormatClaim(formatName);
  const probeClaim = getProbeFormatClaim(formatName);

  if (bookClaim === LedgerClaim.Accepted || probeClaim === LedgerClaim.Accepted) {
    return LedgerClaim.Accepted;
  }

  return probeClaim === LedgerClaim.Unknown ? bookClaim : probeClaim;
}
--- facts
The book took a posting format through the posting interface long before the probe reported the same format.
